@lang en

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version] (פקודת מס הכנסה [נוסח חדש]), s 66 —
-- "חישוב נפרד", separate calculation.  THE NOUNS.
--
-- DECLARE only: no rules, no #EVAL.  Every other module of this row imports
-- this one.  The membership test is the one the encoding skill sets: could a
-- witness of ordinary competence testify to the fact, or does answering it
-- need the Ordinance?  Only the first kind is here.  Where s 66 points at
-- another section whose answer a caller supplies (s 37 entitlement, the value
-- of a credit point, the tax on income from personal exertion), that answer is
-- a GIVEN of the rule that needs it, not a field here, except where it is a
-- fact about one spouse that several rules read (s 37, below).
--
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt
-- (Hebrew Wikisource, retrieved 2026-10-06, sha256 b87f2cf4...94b81b6),
-- s 66 at lines 2454-2484.  Hebrew is authoritative; the file is an
-- unofficial consolidation.  Hebrew strings in comments are copied from it.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 66 — the nouns`

-- "האשה" (s 66(c)(4)) and "הגבר" (s 66(c)(5)).  The section speaks of THE
-- woman and THE man of a couple; see fork F9 in NOTES.md for a couple that is
-- not one of each.
DECLARE `Sex` IS ONE OF
    `a woman`
    `a man`

-- Which of the two spouses a rule is asked about.  "בן הזוג הרשום" is fixed
-- under s 64B, outside this slice, and is a recorded status: an input.
-- The constructors drop the article so they cannot be confused with the
-- fields of `Spouses in a tax year` that carry each spouse's particulars.
DECLARE `Which spouse` IS ONE OF
    `registered spouse`
    `spouse who is not the registered spouse`

-- s 66(a)(1): "הכנסתו מיגיעה אישית בעסק או משלח יד או מעבודה, לרבות הכנסתו
-- מיגיעה אישית כאמור בפסקאות (1) עד (7) להגדרתה שבסעיף 1".  The first two are
-- the body of the phrase; the other eight are the paragraphs of the s 1
-- definition of "הכנסה מיגיעה אישית" (lines 170-178), named for what they are,
-- with the paragraph number in a comment.
DECLARE `Kind of income from personal exertion` IS ONE OF
    `from a business or profession`
    `from employment`
    `a pension paid by a former employer`                                           -- s 1 def. para (1), line 171
    `a pension from a pension provident fund`                                       -- para (2), line 172
    `a pension paid to the survivors of a person within paragraph (1) or (2)`       -- para (3), line 173
    `a pension for loss of working capacity`                                        -- para (3A), line 174
    `a taxable pension paid by the National Insurance Institute`                    -- para (4), line 175
    `a grant received on retirement or on death`                                    -- para (5), line 176
    `a sum received on the commutation of a pension within paragraphs (1) to (4)`   -- para (6), line 177
    `rent from an asset used for ten years to produce income from personal exertion` -- para (7), line 178

-- One item of a spouse's taxable income from personal exertion.  The two
-- BOOLEANs are the facts the pension proviso of s 66(a)(1) turns on; they are
-- read only for an item that is a pension.  Each is a fact about an earlier
-- year (a recorded entitlement), not a rule this slice runs.
DECLARE `An item of income from personal exertion` HAS
    `kind`           IS A `Kind of income from personal exertion`
    `taxable amount` IS A NUMBER
    `paid in respect of employment income for which the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation, in the five years before the pension began, for the income by virtue of which it is paid`
        IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `A spouse` HAS
    `sex`                                            IS A `Sex`
    `income from personal exertion`                  IS A LIST OF `An item of income from personal exertion`
    -- Taxable income not from personal exertion, OTHER THAN the s 66(b)
    -- property income in the next two fields.
    `taxable income not from personal exertion`      IS A NUMBER
    -- s 66(b): "הכנסה מרכוש שהיה בבעלותו שנה לפני נישואיו"
    `taxable income from property owned one year before the marriage`  IS A NUMBER
    -- s 66(b): "או מרכוש שקיבל בירושה בתקופת נישואיו"
    `taxable income from property inherited during the marriage`       IS A NUMBER
    -- The two claims ("רשאי לתבוע", "רשאי ... לבקש") are elections: facts.
    `claims a separate calculation of the tax on income from personal exertion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `claims a separate calculation of the tax on the property income in subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 66(c)(4A) "אישה שנישאה לאלמן"; (c)(6) "גבר שנישא לאלמנה".
    `a widow or widower when the present marriage was contracted` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 37 (line 1600) is outside this slice: whether this spouse is a
    -- "יחיד מוטב" who has proved the maintenance of the other spouse, and so
    -- would have one credit point under s 37, is a GIVEN.  s 66(c)(2) cuts it
    -- to one half.
    `would be entitled to a credit point under section 37` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Version 0.2.0 (02-R2).  s 48A, line 1811: "”עובד זר“ – כהגדרתו בחוק
    -- עובדים זרים ... אף אם רואים אותו כתושב לענין פקודה זו".  A fact about the
    -- spouse, as row IL-01 takes it on `Individual` (`a foreign worker`); named
    -- apart from IL-01's field so the two cannot collide in one import scope
    -- (NOTES.md section 9).  Read only for the half point s 66(c)(4) gives
    -- under s 36A; see ito66-c-credit-points.l4.
    `a foreign worker within the meaning of section 48A` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Version 0.4.0 (fork F20, inventory 01-F1, shared with row IL-01).
    -- Whether the spouse counts as an Israeli resident in the tax year, as row
    -- IL-01 decides it (s 1, or s 3A(f)).  s 66 does not test residence; it is
    -- read only for the half point (c)(4) gives under s 36A, where it matters
    -- only if s 36A has a residence condition.  Named apart from IL-01's
    -- `an Israeli resident in the tax year` so the two cannot collide.
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year, for section 36A` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A child of either spouse, or of both.
-- Version 0.2.0 (02-N3): named `A child` until 0.1.0; qualified so that one
-- module can name it beside row IL-06's child (IL-07 RECONCILE.md N3).
DECLARE `A child, for section 66` HAS
    -- s 40(b)(3), incorporated by s 66(c)(4)(a): "שנת לידה" is the tax year in
    -- which the child was born.  The child's age in a tax year is that tax year
    -- less this one.
    `tax year of birth`                              IS A NUMBER
    `a child of the registered spouse`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `a child of the spouse who is not the registered spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 66(c)(4)(a1): the mother's election to count one birth-year credit
    -- point in the following tax year instead.
    `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 66(a)(3): the child's income from the four sources it names.
    `taxable income from a transparent company`      IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income from a real estate investment trust` IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income from interest`                   IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income from capital gain`               IS A NUMBER

-- s 66(d)(2): "מקור הכנסה של בן זוג התלוי במקור ההכנסה של בן הזוג השני".
-- Whether the spouses have one at all is the MAYBE on `Spouses in a tax year`;
-- these are the facts s 66(d)(1)(a)-(c) asks of it.
DECLARE `A common source of income` HAS
    `the personal exertion of each spouse is required to produce the income` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(1)(a)
    `each spouse receives income matching his contribution to producing it`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(1)(b), first limb
    `each spouse's income stands in direct proportion to his contribution`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(1)(b), second limb
    `produced in the spouses' residence`                                     IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(1)(c), the gate
    `the residence serves the common source permanently`                     IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(1)(c)
    `most of the activity of the source is carried on in the residence`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(1)(c)
    -- Version 0.4.0 (fork F1, reading (ii)): how much of the taxable income
    -- from personal exertion of the spouse who is not the registered spouse
    -- comes from this source.  NOTHING where the facts do not say; only the
    -- reading that shuts subsection (a) for this income alone needs it.
    `the income from personal exertion it gives the spouse who is not the registered spouse, if known` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- THE READINGS (version 0.4.0, BACKLOG IL-47).  Meng ruled on 2026-10-08
-- (SHRUG) that where the text is silent each fork is one named switch,
-- default DECLINE where its readings give different answers, every other
-- reading kept by name and tested.  The switches themselves are rules in the
-- module of the provision (`... — the reading this row takes ...`).
--
-- A reading is not a fact a witness could testify to, so these types break
-- this module's membership test.  They are here because `Spouses in a tax
-- year` carries the readings a caller asks for (its last field, NOTHING for
-- this row's switches), and that record is declared here.  Carrying them on
-- the couple lets every rule that takes the couple see the same readings
-- without a reading argument threaded through each of them.  NOTES.md,
-- "Version 0.4.0".
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Fork F1, s 66(d)(1), line 2479.
DECLARE `A reading of section 66(d)(1) where a common source of income fails its conditions` IS ONE OF
    `subsection (a) does not apply to the spouses at all`                        -- (i), versions 0.1.0-0.3.0
    `subsection (a) does not apply to the income from the common source alone`   -- (ii)
    `declined where the readings of section 66(d)(1) differ`                     -- the default

-- Fork F6, s 66(a)(3), line 2458, with s 65's exception, line 2448.
DECLARE `A reading of section 66(a)(3) as to the exception in section 65` IS ONE OF
    `section 65's exception does not apply under (a)(3)`                        -- (i), versions 0.1.0-0.3.0
    `section 65's exception applies under (a)(3)`                                -- (ii)
    `declined where the readings of the exception in section 65 differ`          -- the default

-- Fork F14, s 66(a)(2) with (a)(3), lines 2457-2458.
DECLARE `A reading of section 66(a)(3) where (a)(2) sends the pooled income to the spouse who is not the registered spouse` IS ONE OF
    `the children's income stays with the registered spouse`                     -- (i), versions 0.1.0-0.3.0
    `the children's income goes with the pooled income`                          -- (ii)
    `declined where the readings of the children's income and the pool differ`   -- the default

-- Fork F7, the proviso to s 66(b), line 2459.
DECLARE `A reading of the proviso to section 66(b) as to the registered spouse` IS ONE OF
    `only the separate calculation under (a)(1) is other income for which a separate calculation is made`   -- (i), versions 0.1.0-0.3.0
    `the registered spouse's own calculation counts once (a)(1) or (c)(1A) makes a separate calculation`     -- (ii)
    `declined where the readings of the proviso to section 66(b) differ`                                     -- the default

-- Fork F18, s 66(c)(1A), line 2462.
DECLARE `A reading of section 66(c)(1A) as to the registered spouse` IS ONE OF
    `the registered spouse may request under (c)(1A)`                            -- (i), versions 0.1.0-0.3.0
    `only the spouse who is not the registered spouse may request under (c)(1A)` -- (ii)
    `declined where the readings of (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse differ`  -- the default

-- Fork F8, s 66(c)(1A), line 2462, with s 66(d)(1), line 2479.
DECLARE `A reading of section 66(c)(1A) where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a request under (c)(1A) is not shut by subsection (d)`                      -- (i), versions 0.1.0-0.3.0
    `a request under (c)(1A) is shut by subsection (d)`                          -- (ii)
    `declined where the readings of (c)(1A) and subsection (d) differ`           -- the default

-- Fork F20, s 66(c)(4), line 2465, with s 36A, line 1597 (inventory 01-F1;
-- row IL-01's fork F1).
DECLARE `A reading of section 36A on residence, for section 66(c)(4)` IS ONE OF
    `the half point under section 36A without a residence condition`             -- (i), versions 0.1.0-0.3.0
    `the half point under section 36A only for an Israeli resident`              -- (ii)
    `declined where residence decides the half point under section 36A`          -- the default

DECLARE `Readings of section 66 for a couple` HAS
    `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`              IS A `A reading of section 66(d)(1) where a common source of income fails its conditions`
    `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)`                              IS A `A reading of section 66(a)(3) as to the exception in section 65`
    `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse` IS A `A reading of section 66(a)(3) where (a)(2) sends the pooled income to the spouse who is not the registered spouse`
    `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse`                       IS A `A reading of the proviso to section 66(b) as to the registered spouse`
    `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`                                 IS A `A reading of section 66(c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`
    `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)`                           IS A `A reading of section 66(c)(1A) where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`
    `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)`                             IS A `A reading of section 36A on residence, for section 66(c)(4)`

DECLARE `Spouses in a tax year` HAS
    `tax year`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the registered spouse`                          IS A `A spouse`
    `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`    IS A `A spouse`
    `children`                                       IS A LIST OF `A child, for section 66`
    -- s 66(d)(1) "בני זוג שיש להם מקור הכנסה משותף": the source names the
    -- case where there is none, so NOTHING is an answer, not a gap.
    `common source of income`                        IS A MAYBE `A common source of income`
    -- Version 0.4.0 (fork F6).  s 65, line 2448: "אלא אם כן הנכסים שמהם היתה
    -- ההכנסה מריבית, מקרן להשקעות במקרקעין או מרווח הון, התקבלו בירושה, או
    -- שמקורם בפיצויים או בכספי ביטוח שהתקבלו בשל פגיעת גוף".  Of the income of
    -- the registered spouse's children within (a)(3), the part from interest, a
    -- real estate investment trust or capital gain whose assets came that way.
    -- One sum for the children, on the couple rather than on each child, so
    -- that the existing constructions of `A child, for section 66` (the
    -- independent tests' among them) need no new field; 0 where there is none.
    `of the children's income within (a)(3), the part from assets received by inheritance or from compensation or insurance for bodily injury` IS A NUMBER
    -- Version 0.4.0: the readings to take, or NOTHING for this row's switches.
    `the readings of section 66 to take, if not this row's` IS A MAYBE `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
